{
 "about": "Fresh blind set for TestRetrievalQuality, built 2026-11-22 for one decision: which of the ranking ideas (larger per-retriever pools, an OR top-up for BM25, weighted RRF) and the question-style summaries to keep. 23 queries on themes and phrasings neither other set covers, written before any ranking was run. Candidates: the top 10 of every ranking variant tried (shipped fusion; pools of 75-200; OR top-up; RRF weights 0.5-1 either way; BM25-only AND and OR; vector-only) on two builds (D, and E2 with regenerated pilot summaries), plus a title lookup over the non-Discord sources; judged from title, summary and excerpts, sorted by doc_id without knowing which ranking proposed them (E2's 16 extra candidates were judged in a second pass). key = the direct answer, relevant = helps. Built against the 68,457-doc corpus of build D. Added 2026-11-22: the top 10 of three chunking variants (300-char chunks; token-sized chunks with the head on each; a head-only vector plus title-prefixed chunks; each fused as shipped, with BM25 x 0.75, and vector-only) were pooled the same way, and the never-judged docs among them judged blind, sorted by doc_id. Added 2026-11-23: the top 10 of builds whose code sources (source-scripts, source-dump, source-workspace, defs-bo3) carry generated summaries, ranked as one list and with the code ranked apart (7 pages, then 3 code files; BM25 x 0.5, 0.75 and 1), were pooled the same way, and the never-judged docs among them judged blind.",
